   "text": "I read the structure left to right from the C-terminal leucine, then wrote it as SMILES.\n\n**Peptide chain (C-terminus to the Arg-containing linkage):**\n- Leu with a free COOH, then Pro, Ser (CH2OH side chain), cyclohexylalanine, Gly, 4-hydroxyproline and Pro.\n- The Pro is acylated by an arginine-type residue whose \u03b1-carbon carries an O (not an NH). This O forms an ester with the carbonyl of the next residue, so the linkage is a depsipeptide ester.\n- The arginine side chain is CH2CH2CH2NHC(=NH)NH2.\n\n**Linker and tail:**\n- The ester carbonyl belongs to a lysine residue with a free 4-aminobutyl side chain (CH2)4NH2.\n- Its \u03b1-NH is acylated by C(=O)CH2 attached to the nitrogen of a piperidine ring.\n- The piperidine 4-NH forms an amide with an azido-lysine-derived residue. That residue has a chain of four CH2 groups ending at N1 of a 1,2,3-triazole.\n- Triazole C4 carries CH2\u2013N\u207a(CH3)2\u2013CH2\u2013BF3\u207b. The BF3 sits on a single carbon, so this is an ammoniomethyl trifluoroborate.\n- The \u03b1-NH of the azido-lysine residue is acylated by C(=O)CH2 on one nitrogen of a DOTA macrocycle (cyclen with three CH2COOH arms).\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned each wedge or hash centre from the drawing by CIP priorities. Every stereocentre comes out as the L-type (S) configuration: Leu, both Pro residues, Ser, Cha, Hyp, the O-substituted Arg unit, Lys and the azido-Lys unit. The hydroxyl-bearing carbon of Hyp is drawn with plain bonds, so it carries no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)[C@H](CC(C)C)NC(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](CO)NC(=O)[C@H](CC1CCCCC1)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H]1CC(O)CN1C(=O)[C@@H]1CCCN1C(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(N)=N)OC(=O)[C@H](CCCCN)NC(=O)CN1CCC(CC1)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCCn1cc(C[N+](C)(C)C[B-](F)(F)F)nn1)NC(=O)CN1CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)O)CC1"
  }
